KJV renders: open.

H6359.strongs:
Origin: from 6362;
Meaning: open, i.e. unoccupied
KJV renders: free.

H6360.strongs:
Origin: intensively from an unused root meaning to pound;
Meaning: a hammer
KJV renders: hammer.

H6361.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to that of 6360;
Meaning: a gown (as if hammered out wide)
KJV renders: hose.

H6362.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to cleave or burst through, i.e. (causatively) to emit, whether literal or figurative (gape)
KJV renders: dismiss, free, let (shoot) out, slip away.

H6363.strongs:
Origin: or פִּטְרָה; from 6362;
Meaning: a fissure, i.e. (concretely) firstling (as opening the matrix)
KJV renders: firstling, openeth, such as open.

H6364.strongs:
Origin: of Egyptian origin;
Meaning: Pi-Beseth, a place in Egypt
KJV renders: Pi-beseth.

H6365.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root probably meaning to pierce;
Meaning: (figuratively) misfortune
KJV renders: destruction, ruin.

H6366.strongs:
Origin: or פִּיָּה; feminine of 6310;
Meaning: an edge
KJV renders: (two-) edge(-d).

H6367.strongs:
Origin: from 6310 and the feminine plural of a noun (from the same root as 2356), with the article interpolated; mouth of the gorges;
Meaning: Pi-ha-Chiroth, a place in Egypt
KJV renders: Pi-hahiroth. (In Numbers 14:19 without Pi-.)

H6368.strongs:
Origin: from 6315;
Meaning: a powder (as easily puffed away), i.e. ashes or dust
KJV renders: ashes.

H6369.strongs:
Origin: apparently from 6310 and 3605; mouth of all;
Meaning: Picol, a Philistine
KJV renders: Phichol.

H6370.strongs:
Origin: or פִּלֶגֶשׁ; of uncertain derivation;
Meaning: a concubine; also (masculine) a paramour
KJV renders: concubine, paramour.

H6371.strongs:
Origin: probably from an unused root meaning to be plump;
Meaning: obesity
KJV renders: collops.

H6372.strongs:
Origin: apparently from 6310 and a variation of 5175; mouth of a serpent;
Meaning: Pinechas, the name of three Israelites
KJV renders: Phinehas.

H6373.strongs:
Origin: probably the same as 6325;
Meaning: Pinon, an Idumaean
KJV renders: Pinon.

H6374.strongs:
Origin: for 6366;
Meaning: an edge or tooth
KJV renders: tooth, × two-edged.

H6375.strongs:
Origin: from 6329;
Meaning: a tottering
KJV renders: smite together.

H6376.strongs:
Origin: from 6335; dispersive;
Meaning: Pishon, a river of Eden
KJV renders: Pison.

H6377.strongs:
Origin: probably from the same as 6596; expansive;
Meaning: Pithon, an Israelite
KJV renders: Pithon.

H6378.strongs:
Origin: from 6379;
Meaning: a flask (from which a liquid may flow)
KJV renders: box, vial.

H6379.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to pour
KJV renders: run out.

H6380.strongs:
Origin: from the active participle (of the same form as the first word) feminine of an unused root (meaning to entrap) and plural of 6643; trap of gazelles;
Meaning: Pokereth-Tsebajim, one of the 'servants of Solomon'
KJV renders: Pochereth of Zebaim.

H6381.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, perhaps to separate, i.e. distinguish (literally or figuratively); by implication, to be (causatively, make) great, difficult, wonderful
KJV renders: accomplish, (arise...too, be too) hard, hidden, things too high, (be, do, do a, shew) marvelous(-ly, -els, things, work), miracles, perform, separate, make singular, (be, great, make) wonderful(-ers, -ly, things, works), wondrous (things, works, -ly).

H6382.strongs:
Origin: from 6381;
Meaning: a miracle
KJV renders: marvellous thing, wonder(-ful, -fully).

H6383.strongs:
Origin: or פָּלִיא; from 6381;
Meaning: remarkable
KJV renders: secret, wonderful.

H6384.strongs:
Origin: patronymically from 6396;
Meaning: a Palluite (collectively) or descendants of Pallu
KJV renders: Palluites.

H6385.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to split (literally or figuratively)
KJV renders: divide.

H6387.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) from 6386;
Meaning: a half
KJV renders: dividing.

H6388.strongs:
Origin: from 6385;
Meaning: a rill (i.e. small channel of water, as in irrigation)
KJV renders: river, stream.

H6389.strongs:
Origin: the same as 6388; earthquake;
Meaning: Peleg, a son of Shem
KJV renders: Peleg.

H6390.strongs:
Origin: from 6385;
Meaning: a runlet, i.e. gully
KJV renders: division, river.

H6391.strongs:
Origin: from 6385;
Meaning: a section
KJV renders: division.

H6393.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to divide;
Meaning: a cleaver, i.e. iron armature (of a chariot)
KJV renders: torch.

H6394.strongs:
Origin: of uncertain derivation;
Meaning: Pildash, a relative of Abraham
KJV renders: Pildash.

H6395.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to distinguish (literally or figuratively)
KJV renders: put a difference, show marvellous, separate, set apart, sever, make wonderfully.

H6396.strongs:
Origin: from 6395; distinguished;
Meaning: Pallu, an Israelite
KJV renders: Pallu, Phallu.

H6397.strongs:
Origin: patronymically from an unused name (from 6395) meaning separate;
Meaning: a Pelonite or inhabitant of an unknown Palon
KJV renders: Pelonite.

H6398.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to slice, i.e. break open or pierce
KJV renders: bring forth, cleave, cut, shred, strike through.

H6399.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 6398;
Meaning: to serve or worship
KJV renders: minister, serve.
